JENKINS INSTALLATION NOTES
Ubuntu and RHEL

1. PREREQUISITES
- Ubuntu Server or RHEL Server
- sudo/root access
- Internet connectivity
- Java 21
- Jenkins uses port 8080

Check OS:
  cat /etc/os-release

Check IP:
  hostname -I


2. UBUNTU INSTALLATION

Step 1: Update packages
  sudo apt update
  sudo apt upgrade -y

Step 2: Install Java
  sudo apt install fontconfig openjdk-21-jre -y
  java -version

Step 3: Add Jenkins repository
  sudo wget -O /etc/apt/keyrings/jenkins-keyring.asc   https://pkg.jenkins.io/debian-stable/jenkins.io-2026.key

  echo "deb [signed-by=/etc/apt/keyrings/jenkins-keyring.asc] https://pkg.jenkins.io/debian-stable binary/" | sudo tee /etc/apt/sources.list.d/jenkins.list > /dev/null

  sudo apt update

Step 4: Install Jenkins
  sudo apt install jenkins -y

Step 5: Start and enable Jenkins
  sudo systemctl enable --now jenkins

Step 6: Check status
  sudo systemctl status jenkins

Step 7: Configure firewall (if UFW is enabled)
  sudo ufw allow 8080/tcp
  sudo ufw status

Step 8: Get initial password
  sudo cat /var/lib/jenkins/secrets/initialAdminPassword

Step 9: Open Jenkins
  http://SERVER_IP:8080


3. RHEL INSTALLATION

Step 1: Update packages
  sudo dnf update -y

Step 2: Install Java
  sudo dnf install java-21-openjdk -y
  java -version

Step 3: Add Jenkins repository
  sudo wget -O /etc/yum.repos.d/jenkins.repo   https://pkg.jenkins.io/redhat-stable/jenkins.repo

  sudo rpm --import https://pkg.jenkins.io/redhat-stable/jenkins.io-2026.key

  sudo dnf clean all
  sudo dnf makecache

Step 4: Install Jenkins
  sudo dnf install jenkins -y

Step 5: Start and enable Jenkins
  sudo systemctl enable --now jenkins

Step 6: Check status
  sudo systemctl status jenkins

Step 7: Configure firewalld
  sudo firewall-cmd --permanent --add-port=8080/tcp
  sudo firewall-cmd --reload
  sudo firewall-cmd --list-ports

Step 8: Get initial password
  sudo cat /var/lib/jenkins/secrets/initialAdminPassword

Step 9: Open Jenkins
  http://SERVER_IP:8080


4. JENKINS INITIAL SETUP

1. Open http://SERVER_IP:8080
2. Enter the initial administrator password.
3. Select "Install suggested plugins".
4. Create the first administrator user.
5. Configure the Jenkins URL.
6. Open the Jenkins Dashboard.


5. COMMON JENKINS COMMANDS

Start:
  sudo systemctl start jenkins

Stop:
  sudo systemctl stop jenkins

Restart:
  sudo systemctl restart jenkins

Status:
  sudo systemctl status jenkins

Enable at boot:
  sudo systemctl enable jenkins

View logs:
  sudo journalctl -u jenkins -f

Check port:
  sudo ss -lntp | grep 8080


6. IMPORTANT JENKINS LOCATIONS

Jenkins home:
  /var/lib/jenkins

Jobs:
  /var/lib/jenkins/jobs

Plugins:
  /var/lib/jenkins/plugins

Initial password:
  /var/lib/jenkins/secrets/initialAdminPassword

Default port:
  8080


7. UBUNTU VS RHEL QUICK REFERENCE

Ubuntu:
  Package manager: apt
  Package query: dpkg
  Firewall: ufw

RHEL:
  Package manager: dnf
  Package query: rpm
  Firewall: firewalld

Both:
  Service manager: systemd
  Jenkins service: jenkins
  Jenkins port: 8080
  Jenkins home: /var/lib/jenkins


8. BASIC TROUBLESHOOTING

Check Jenkins status:
  sudo systemctl status jenkins

Check logs:
  sudo journalctl -u jenkins -xe

Check Java:
  java -version

Check port:
  sudo ss -lntp | grep 8080

Test locally:
  curl http://localhost:8080

Check Ubuntu firewall:
  sudo ufw status

Check RHEL firewall:
  sudo firewall-cmd --list-ports
